  *      close it with USBC opcode CONTROL1_WRITE = COM_USB, bit-banged I2C.
  * The controller is then set up by sweet_usb_gadget_start, high speed only
  * (the UTMI clock feeds the absent SS PHY's pipe side, s9_dwc3_global).
+ *
+ * OnePlus 6 (/chosen/sweet-board = "oneplus,enchilada", same SDM845): it is
+ * always started with `fastboot boot`, so ABL's fastboot gadget ran on this
+ * controller. sweetusb=1 on the phone (op6-B2 log) showed what ABL leaves:
+ * GDSC and all seven clocks on, DWC3 3.00a in device mode, DCTL run/stop 0
+ * and DSTS halted (ABL already disconnected from the PC), last link
+ * SuperSpeed (DCFG/DSTS speed 4: ABL used the QMP SS PHY), and the QUSB2 PHY
+ * powered down (PWR_CTRL1 0x23 = Linux's disable_ctrl VREF_SUPPLY_TRIM |
+ * CLAMP_N_EN | POWER_DOWN, PLL not ready) with ABL's tuning still in place.
+ * op6_usb_start therefore: RPMh votes for the OP6 PHY rails (mainline
+ * sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi usb_1_hsphy; live DT ldo1/ldo12/ldo24: L1A 0.88 V,
+ * L12A 1.8 V, L24A 3.088 V) and the same bus votes, TBU GDSC votes and SMMU stream 0x740 as
+ * the S9 (live DT usb@a600000 iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x740 0>), GCC only if ABL
+ * left it off, the PHY powered up as the last step of Linux's
+ * qusb2_phy_init (a full re-init only if its PLL does not lock), the UTMI
+ * clock for the pipe side (DT qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk), then the same
+ * gadget. No MAX77705 (the OP6 has none: its GPIOs 33/34 are not that bus).
  */
 #define S9_RSC_PA               0x179e0000u
 #define S9_TCS_PA               0x179e0d00u
@@ -152,7 +170,27 @@ static const uint16_t s9_qusb2_init[] = {      /* qcom,qusb-phy-init-seq: value,
 
